---
title: Drunkard’s walk
---
A digger staggers at random through solid rock, and more follow until enough of the map is open [[t:87-97 s:11]].

## The rule
1. Start with a solid map [[c04:17-19]].
2. **First digger:** starts at the center of the map [[c04:21-22]].
3. **A digger,** again and again [[c04:54-57]]:
   1. steps one tile in a random direction [[c04:58-64]];
   2. digs the tile it lands on [[c04:64-66]];
   3. stops when it steps off the map, or once its step count is over 200 [[c04:65-74]].
4. **While less than a third of the map is open:** start another digger on a random open tile [[c04:25-47]].

- **Talk says:** each new digger spawns somewhere within the open map. Stop when enough of the map is open: a third, here [[t:95-97]].

## Step through it
@@steps limit=5 mid=1

## Controls
@@control lifetime
Steps a digger takes. The demo stops a digger once its step count is over 200 [[c04:54-76]].
@@control floor_divisor
Diggers keep coming until 1 / this of the map’s tiles are open. The demo: a third [[c04:25 t:96-97]].

## What it produces, measured
@@measured

- **Talk says:** guaranteed to be contiguous [[t:99-100]].
- **Drunkard’s walk:** holds. {{c04.regions.max}} region on every seed [[run:c04.regions.max]].
- **Passages:** wide. Corridor ratio {{c04.corridor_ratio.median}} at the median, vs cellular automata’s {{c03.corridor_ratio.median}} [[run:c04.corridor_ratio.median c03.corridor_ratio.median]].

## Where it fails
@@fails

- **No cap in the talk’s code:** its loop of diggers ends only when the open share is reached [[c04:25-48]].

## What it combines with
@@combines

- **Talk’s use:** limestone caverns and similar [[t:100-102]].

